Source provenance notes

The direct builder's cache contains redacted compiler outputs of project-authored
helpers. Matching factory spans are zero placeholders and are restored only from
the user's verified factory input. Source/include and restored-object hashes,
compiler metadata and extraction provenance are retained under
firmware_builder/direct/. The derived publication manifest is distinguished from
the original recording; it does not claim a new compiler recording. Content audits
and provenance checks do not independently certify authorship or grant rights to
manufacturer firmware.

The MIT grant in LICENSE applies to this repository's own source files,
including files retaining older GPL-2.0-or-later SPDX comments. This grant
supersedes those project license headers. The headers are retained to preserve
the exact source bytes pinned by the firmware tooling and evidence inventories.
This does not replace or extend third-party licensing terms.

The B13 boottrace sha.inc file contains 32 bytes of baseline application
SHA-256 data, referenced by trace.asm; it is not a SHA implementation.
The B16 VerifyB16Words.java and VerifyGeometryWords.java files are
project-specific Ghidra verification scripts. They use Ghidra APIs; no
Ghidra implementation source is included in those files. The B16
native_mapper_test.cpp copies are project-specific ELF execution fixtures.
Inspection found no third-party attribution or license notices in these
helpers. This records the retained evidence, not an independent authorship
certification. Report any missing attribution through a repository issue.
